REPAIRAGENT-OCI THOUGHTS: [0m The inspected cgroup_deprecated.go shows runc aliases libcontainer resource types directly to github.com/opencontainers/cgroups.Resources, so the faulty cgroup v1 shares to v2 weight conversion is likely not implemented in this alias file itself. The reproduction sets linux.resources.cpu.shares=1024, and the observed bad behavior is cpu.weight=39 rather than 100 on cgroup v2. Since the cgroups dependency owns Resources and cgroup file writing, the likely runc-side fix must be in the OCI spec conversion path where LinuxCPU.Shares is copied into cgroups.Resources, or in a local override/compatibility path before cgroup v2 is written. I should inspect libcontainer/specconv/spec_linux.go around CPU resource conversion to see exactly how OCI CPU shares are transferred.
